.SH What \[lq]paragraph under cursor\[rq] means
Lines from the previous blank line down to the next blank line (matches
\f[CR]{\f[R] / \f[CR]}\f[R] Vim motions).
The whole paragraph is sent as a single multi\-line command \[em] useful
for one\-shot REPL fragments, SQL statements, or shell scripts.
.SH Sending a visual selection
In any visual mode (\f[CR]v\f[R], \f[CR]V\f[R], \f[CR]<C\-v>\f[R]),
\f[CR]<space>ts\f[R] (or \f[CR]:tmux_send_selection\f[R]) sends the
highlighted text to the last focused tmux pane and exits visual mode.
Character\-, line\-, and block\-wise selections are all joined with
newlines, matching the behaviour of \f[CR]:tmux_send_line\f[R] for
paragraphs.
.SH Requirements
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]tmux\f[R] on \f[CR]$PATH\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
hed must itself be running inside a tmux session (otherwise there is no
current pane to split off from)
.PP
If tmux isn\[cq]t available, the commands fail with a status\-line
message and the rest of the editor keeps working.
.SH Notes
.IP \[bu] 2
The runner pane is just a tmux pane with a shell \[em] anything
interactive (REPLs, \f[CR]htop\f[R], \f[CR]man\f[R]) works.
\f[CR]:tmux_send\f[R] is literally \f[CR]tmux send\-keys\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
Add \f[CR]set \-as terminal\-features \[aq],alacritty:sync\[aq]\f[R] (or
your outer\- terminal equivalent) to your \f[CR]\[ti]/.tmux.conf\f[R] so
synchronized\-output escapes propagate from hed through tmux.
Without it tmux consumes the sync escape itself, which is harmless but
means flicker reduction stops at tmux.
